---
import ServiceGuide from '../components/ServiceGuide.astro';
const URL_ = 'https://liverpoolemergencyplumber.co.uk/frozen-condensate-pipe-liverpool';
const TEL = 'tel:01515580334';
const PHONE = '0151 558 0334';

const faqs = [
  { q: 'How do I know if my condensate pipe is frozen?', a: 'It is freezing outside, the boiler makes a gurgling noise, then it stops and shows a fault code. The plastic pipe outside may have ice at the end. If all three happen together, a frozen condensate pipe is the most likely cause.' },
  { q: 'Can I pour boiling water on a frozen condensate pipe?', a: 'No. Boiling water can crack the plastic pipe and can scald you. Use warm water, like you would use for washing up, or a hot water bottle.' },
  { q: 'Where is my condensate pipe?', a: 'It is a white or grey plastic pipe, about the width of a thumb, that runs from the bottom of the boiler through the wall to a drain or gully outside. Some run inside to a sink waste instead, and those rarely freeze.' },
  { q: 'How long does it take to thaw a condensate pipe?', a: 'Usually 10 to 20 minutes with warm water. Pour slowly along the pipe, especially at bends and the open end, then reset the boiler.' },
  { q: 'My boiler still will not work after thawing. What now?', a: 'Reset the boiler once more. If it still locks out, the pipe may be frozen inside the wall or the fault may be something else. Call us on 0151 558 0334. The first hour is £120 on weekdays and there is no call-out fee.' },
  { q: 'Can you stop it freezing again?', a: 'Yes. We can lag the outside run, fit a wider pipe outside, shorten the outside run, or re-route it inside to a waste pipe. We look at your pipe and tell you the price before we start.' },
  { q: 'How much does it cost to fix a frozen condensate pipe?', a: 'Our first hour is £120 on weekdays from 9am to 4pm, £150 in the evenings, at night and at weekends, and £180 on bank holidays. There is no call-out fee. Thawing and resetting usually fits inside the first hour.' },
  { q: 'Is a frozen condensate pipe dangerous?', a: 'No. The boiler shuts itself down safely. It is a nuisance, not a gas danger. If you smell gas, that is different: call 0800 111 999 straight away.' },
  { q: 'Which error codes mean a frozen condensate pipe?', a: 'It often shows as a lighting or lockout fault. For example Baxi E133, Ideal L2, Worcester Bosch EA 227 and Vaillant F28 or F29. These codes can have other causes too, so check the pipe first.' },
  { q: 'Do you come out at night for this?', a: 'Yes, 24/7. A real person answers. Many people prefer to try the warm water fix first, and we are happy to talk you through it on the phone.' },
];
---

